fsim toolchain 22.1.8-1 (LLVM 22.1.8, x86-64 Windows, UCRT)

fsim is built for Windows with this toolchain, and fsim's Windows binary
archives install its redistributable archive,
fsim-toolchain-22.1.8-1-ucrt-x86_64-redist.zip, unmodified beside fsim, so
plug-ins can be compiled with the same compiler and C++ runtime and debugged.

The toolchain is built from https://github.com/colinphill/fsim-toolchain
(tag fsim-22.1.8-1), a fork of LLVM-MinGW 20260616 by Martin Storsjo that
targets only x86_64-w64-mingw32 and omits Python, clang-tools-extra and
lldb-mi. It contains:

  LLVM Project 22.1.8: clang, lld, LLDB, libc++, libunwind, compiler-rt and
  the shared libLLVM-22.dll, licensed under the Apache License v2.0 with
  LLVM Exceptions. The adjacent LICENSE reproduces the archive's LICENSE.TXT
  unchanged, including the legacy University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source
  License.

  mingw-w64 (commit c28e9555bb8800c53449f42a465ad9a5676fce88): headers, CRT
  and import libraries, and winpthreads. Most of mingw-w64 is under the Zope
  Public License 2.1, with parts in the public domain or under BSD, MIT or
  LGPL terms as marked. The license texts are installed with the toolchain in
  x86_64-w64-mingw32/share/mingw32 (COPYING, COPYING.MinGW-w64.txt,
  COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime.txt, COPYING.winpthreads.txt,
  COPYING.winstorecompat.txt).

  LLVM-MinGW wrapper programs and scripts, under the ISC license.

The redistributable archive omits the GPL- and LGPL-licensed build tools of
the full toolchain (BusyBox, GNU make, widl and gendef).

